Farzapedia champions four crucial properties of modern knowledge engineering:
Fetch each locked source, resolve the current HEAD (or the configured ref), and compare against the pinned commit in `wiki.lock`. If the commit has changed, update the lockfile entry.
Fetch external data sources (git repositories with wiki pages or RDF data), resolve commit SHAs, and pin them in `wiki.lock`. Without arguments, installs all sources declared in the `sources:` block of `wiki.yml`. With a URL, adds the source to `wiki.yml` first, then fetches and locks it.
Files under configured **memory paths** (for example `user.md`, `memory.md`, or custom `--memory-paths`) are distilled and indexed by Supermemory; ordinary paths behave more like a synced file tree.
Files with raw RDF extensions are parsed directly by rdflib using the format mapped from their extension. They bypass all document processing — no route registration, no link validation, no frontmatter coercion. They contribute triples to the same graph but are invisible to `wiki export` (which operates on documents) and `wiki link`.
Find `&lt;!-- sparql:start --&gt;` ... `&lt;!-- sparql:end --&gt;` regions in markdown, run the embedded query against the wiki graph, and rewrite the table (or `(no results)`) in place.
For [wiki build](wiki_build.md) and [wiki serve](wiki_serve.md), set `wazoo:layout` to a page layout path (for example `layouts/article.html`) to override the site default for that page. Omit it to use `site.layout` from `wiki.yml` or `wiki.yaml`. See [Wiki Page Layouts](Wiki_Page_Layouts.md). Infobox values like `wiki:Other_Page` still link when that page exists.
For `dict` and `json-ld`, each entry is `{"name": "<filename>", "rdf": ...}`.
