{
|                          | [wiki](wiki.md)                                              | [Supermemory SMFS](Supermemory_SMFS.md)      | [Letta MemFS](Letta_MemFS.md)               |
|                  |                                                                                                                                                          |
|          | Vector RAG              | GraphRAG                                       |
| **Agent role**    | Gardener — tends and expands the wiki                       | Meta-cognitive — reflects on and improves its own process                   |
| **Always on**       | Behavior not gated by yaml severities (route safety, URL collisions, built-in RDF prefixes).                                                                            |
| **Authority**            | Your wiki on disk                                            | Supermemory API                              | Local Git (+ Letta Cloud for API agents)    |
| **Dates**        | 15 May 2026, 5:00 PM – 18 May 2026, 5:00 PM (per [AI Valley listing](https://www.aivalley.io/hackathons/wikithon-build-your-own-wikipedia-with-hydradb)) |
| **Docker / devcontainers** | Supported for mount mode                                                                                                               |
| **Examples**      | Adding a new page, enriching frontmatter, growing the graph | `tropo check` gates in Vivary, `wiki render --check`, receipt-driven review |
| **Execution Context** | Inside the Obsidian application (GUI)    | Terminal, scripts, and CI/CD pipelines          |
| **Format**       | Online; 48-hour build sprint                                                                                                                             |
| **Hot context**          | Agent chooses pages to open                                  | `profile.md` + semantic grep                 | `system/` loaded every turn                 |
| **Init**            | Written by `wiki init` ([`wiki.yml`](https://github.com/wazootech/wiki/blob/main/src/wiki/templates/wiki.yml)); omitting an Init key is the same as the schema default. |
| **Local cache**            | SQLite-backed cache; bidirectional sync (default pull ~30s)                                                                            |
| **Logical Inference** | None (direct field matching)             | OWL-RL reasoning (implicit class hierarchies)   |
| **Metaphor**             | Semantic markdown **wiki** / codebase                        | Cloud container as **mount** or virtual bash | **Git repo** of memory markdown             |
| **Output Formats**    | Dynamic markdown views in Obsidian       | Static HTML, Turtle, JSON-LD, RDF/XML           |
| **Publishing**           | Static site, RDF export                                      | N/A (runtime memory)                         | N/A (agent memory)                          |
| **Query Language**    | DQL (custom SQL-like) or JavaScript      | SPARQL (W3C standard)                           |
| **Recommended**     | Not enforced by schema, but you typically set it for a real wiki (for example `graph.context.wiki`, `wiki.filename_pattern`, `site.layout`).                            |
| **Registration** | [Luma event page](https://luma.com/6pybuh79)                                                                                                             |
| **Risk**          | Stale or contradictory pages if unchecked                   | Infinite loops or over-optimization without gates                           |
| **Scale**         | Sessions to months                                          | Single turn to a few turns                                                  |
| **Schema optional** | Key or block may be omitted; Pydantic applies a default. No yaml key is strictly required for `Config.load()` to succeed.                                               |
| **Search**               | SPARQL, link graph, `wiki query`                             | Semantic `grep` (literal with flags)         | Tree + on-demand file read                  |
| **Status**       | Completed (as listed on AI Valley)                                                                                                                       |
| **Storage model** | Growing corpus of documents and graph triples               | Self-modifying workflows, skills, and memory                                |
| **Storage**                | Supermemory API, semantic graph, hosted vector index                                                                                   |
| **Structured semantics** | YAML-LD, [SHACL](SHACL.md), JSON Schema, [SPARQL](SPARQL.md) | Memory paths + cloud graph                   | `description` frontmatter; optional folders |
| **Surface**                | Mount via **FUSE** (Linux) or **NFSv3 on localhost** (macOS); or `@supermemory/bash` / `supermemory-bash` where mounting is impossible |
| **Time axis**     | Forward accumulation — each session adds                    | Cyclical refinement — each loop re-evaluates                                |
| **Typical user**         | Wiki authors, PKM + semantics                                | Multi-modal, multi-source agents             | Letta Code coding agents                    |
| **Validation**           | `wiki check` (SHACL, JSON Schema, layout)                    | Supermemory indexing rules                   | Git + agent discipline                      |
| **Validation**        | Presentation only (no constraints check) | `wiki check` (SHACL and JSON Schema validation) |
| **Version control**        | No Git as source of truth; durability and history live in the cloud container                                                          |
